      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Hmm; just thought of this; if the VPN is using a metered network while there are unmetered options available, isn\u0027t that the VPN\u0027s \"fault\", rather than the app\u0027s?\n\nI guess the correct wording of this sentence would be: \"If a VPN is using networks other than the default network then...\"\n\nAnd the answer is \"it depends\". Coz, a VPN might choose to do so for numerous reasons (say smart switching, or reliability or performance, or perhaps user chose to go for reliability/performance). What we have in this patch is the best we can do (which is to ensure that app is not charged for data more than it requested for; and the data it requested gets split based on ratio of data usage of underlying networks).\n\n\u003e Would it be confusing to specifically turn off all background metered/mobile data for apps, and find that it still has data usage? (Or does this get covered by the capabilities update changes?)\n\nYeah this gets covered by the capabilities update changes. There is still isActiveNetworkMetered that needs to be fixed (will do that soon).",
